# TODO - Cross-platform native capability runners

## Objective

Implement the version-1 host-capability contract for supported 64-bit Windows,
macOS, and Linux runners on x86-64 and AArch64. Keep adapters outside the guest
and require the same `.malbolge` payload and guest-visible behavior on every
runner. The normalized DOOM C corpus already passes the strict freestanding
compile gate on the intended six target/architecture pairs without OS-selection
macros; the remaining platform work is capability implementation and runtime
validation, not guest-source porting. Runners must not require LLVM/Clang or an
externally installed multimedia development stack merely to execute an already
generated program. The quality and canonical `doom.c` source stages are
complete; this TODO begins at lowering capability calls into the generated
Malbolge artifact and resolving host modules without changing guest bytes.

## Acceptance

- Windows, macOS, and Linux runners on x86-64 and AArch64 implement the same
  versioned capability-frame semantics behind host-only adapters.
- The same `.malbolge` payload/profile passes differential capability fixtures
  on
  every supported runner without guest OS-selection code or host ABI leakage.
- Capability discovery, invalid ranges/frames, unavailable services, host
  failures, blocking/partial progress, startup, and shutdown fail/complete with
  the same declared guest-visible rules across the matrix.
- An already generated guest program runs without LLVM/Clang and without an
  externally installed multimedia development/runtime dependency except where an
  operating-system facility is explicitly part of the runner contract.
- x86-64/AArch64 implementation details remain adapter concerns and do not alter
  VM semantics or the versioned call ABI.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `execution/`, `runtime/`, `vm/`,
  `tests/vm/`, and `benchmarks/interpreter/`.
- Required evidence: one shared capability-vector corpus across all six
  OS/architecture pairs, malformed/unavailable/failure vectors, dependency
  startup checks, cross-runner differential results, and reproducible platform
  identity for measurements.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `versioned-host-capability-call-abi` and
  `native-x86-64-and-aarch64-backends`.

**Generated Malbolge adapter modules.**

Replace `src/interface/command-line/adapter-outbound/adapters/doom/abi.malbolge`
and
`src/interface/command-line/adapter-outbound/adapters/doom/windows.malbolge`
scaffolds with compiler-generated, verified
modules. A capsule that explicitly requires `doom.host.v1` must trigger
automatic
ABI and current-platform adapter resolution during `malbolge
<artifact.malbolge>`;
filename heuristics and implicit capability grants are forbidden.
